@startuml PassTheKeysDefended
title Defended - passkey + DPoP: the relayed session is sender-constrained

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 14
skinparam BoxPadding 12

actor "Victim" as V
box "The website (Acme, defended)" #E7F6EC
  participant "Front-end\nvictim's tab (/login)\n+ PasskeyProvider" as VP
  participant "Relying party\nverifies + binds the session" as RP
end box
box "Attacker's site (separate origin)" #FDECEC
  participant "Attacker's tab" as AP
  participant "Back-end\ndead-drop + proxy" as AD
end box
actor "Attacker" as A

note across
  The victim's browser holds a NON-EXTRACTABLE DPoP keypair (IndexedDB). Its thumbprint jkt
  is folded into the one field the authenticator signs - the challenge (nonce):
      signedChallenge = SHA256( serverNonce + "." + jkt )
  The private key never leaves this browser.
end note

== Attacker starts a login, but will not finish it ==
A -> AP : open the attacker site
AP -> RP : start a passkey login (via proxy)
RP --> AP : nonce **Ca**
AP -> AD : publish **Ca** in the dead-drop

== Victim's page is compromised and relays the sign-in ==
V -> VP : click "Sign in"
VP -> AD : fetch the nonce (cross-origin) -> **Ca**
VP -> VP : jkt = thumbprint(my DPoP key)\nbound = SHA256(**Ca** + "." + jkt)
VP -> V : passkey prompt - sign **bound**
V --> VP : assertion over **bound** (commits to the victim's jkt)
VP -> AD : hand over the assertion + the DPoP **public** key\n(the private key cannot be relayed - non-extractable)

== Attacker finishes the login - and is stuck ==
AP -> AD : take the assertion + public key
AP -> RP : finish the login with them
RP -> RP : SHA256(Ca + "." + jkt) == signed challenge?  yes\nbind the session token to **jkt**
RP --> AP : a real session token for the victim  (bound to jkt)
AP -> RP : GET /api/me  (Authorization: DPoP <token> + a DPoP proof)
note right of AP : the attacker can only sign with ITS OWN key,\nso its proof's thumbprint != the bound jkt
RP --> AP : **401** - proof key is not the bound key
AP -> A : "Session captured - but locked"

note across #E7F6EC
  The token is sender-constrained. Finishing the ceremony is not enough: every resource call
  needs a fresh DPoP proof signed by the key the session is bound to, which lives only in the
  victim's browser. The relayed session is inert for anyone else.
    Swap the key instead? Binding the finish to the attacker's jkt breaks the challenge match
    (SHA256(Ca + "." + jkt_attacker) != the signed challenge), so the login is rejected.
end note

@enduml
